{"id": "city-funded-nonprofits-fund-political-arms", "title": "City-funded charities that send money to political arms", "seconds": 130.7, "voice": "elevenlabs:exurTFaGNF2gnRcPNH8I", "narrator": "Phil", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "f4cf0530575350f3", "words": 426, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "City-funded charities report grants to groups that can lobby and campaign on ballot measures.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.37, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Charities and ballot measures"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 0.98, 1.29, 1.59, 1.7, 1.98, 2.14, 2.3, 2.58, 2.7, 3.17, 3.29, 3.57]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["story[1]", "oneLine"], "text": "The charities list those grants on their tax returns.", "t0": 4.49, "t1": 6.55, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "irs", "kicker": "Form 990", "text": "Schedule I", "mark": "Schedule I"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.52, 0.7, 0.87, 1.14, 1.22, 1.35, 1.6]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["story[1]", "oneLine"], "text": "And how much is that, in all?", "t0": 6.67, "t1": 8.17, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Form 990, Schedule I", "text": "Schedule I reports grants to organizations.", "mark": "grants", "source": "irs"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.2, 0.36, 0.45, 1.02, 1.17]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "oneLine"], "text": "415,000 dollars.", "t0": 8.17, "t1": 9.57, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$415,000", "label": "from City-funded charities to three advocacy organizations"}, "emph": ["415,000"], "wt": [0.04, 0.22, 0.44, 0.74, 1.03]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["status"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding. Each grant is on the charity’s own tax return.", "t0": 10.09, "t1": 13.58, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.27, 0.35, 0.64, 0.82, 0.89, 1.53, 1.76, 2.03, 2.15, 2.24, 2.34, 2.76, 2.94, 3.19]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[0]", "innocent[0]"], "text": "A charity may give its own unrestricted money, within limits, to an advocacy group.", "t0": 13.7, "t1": 17.67, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["a charity, 501(c)(3)", "no election campaigns"], "b": ["an advocacy group, 501(c)(4)", "can lobby, back ballot measures"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.46, 0.58, 0.73, 0.86, 1.12, 1.68, 2.16, 2.45, 2.95, 3.09, 3.19, 3.65]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["story[0]", "innocent[0]"], "text": "That group can lobby and back ballot measures.", "t0": 17.79, "t1": 19.52, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["a charity, 501(c)(3)", "no election campaigns"], "b": ["an advocacy group, 501(c)(4)", "can lobby, back ballot measures"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.38, 0.51, 0.77, 0.87, 1.07, 1.34]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[2]"], "text": "The catch: money is fungible.", "t0": 19.64, "t1": 20.86, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Money is fungible."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.51, 0.72, 0.83]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[2]"], "text": "When a group lives mostly on public grants, only its books show which dollars went.", "t0": 20.98, "t1": 24.48, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Money is fungible."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.18, 0.41, 0.72, 1.03, 1.14, 1.4, 1.97, 2.18, 2.31, 2.54, 2.7, 2.89, 3.22]}, {"scene": "abode", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "links[0]"], "text": "The biggest: Abode Services.", "t0": 24.7, "t1": 26.13, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City departments", "sub": "$74.1 million, fiscal 2019 to 2026"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Abode Services", "sub": "a City-funded charity"}, {"art": "money", "name": "NPH Action Fund", "sub": "an advocacy group"}], "kicker": "From the charity’s own tax return"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.43, 0.77]}, {"scene": "abode", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "links[0]"], "text": "The City paid it 74.1 million dollars from fiscal 2019 to 2026.", "t0": 26.25, "t1": 30.97, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City departments", "sub": "$74.1 million, fiscal 2019 to 2026"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Abode Services", "sub": "a City-funded charity"}, {"art": "money", "name": "NPH Action Fund", "sub": "an advocacy group"}], "kicker": "From the charity’s own tax return"}, "emph": ["74.1 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.47, 0.68, 0.78, 1.29, 1.55, 1.77, 2.08, 2.41, 2.59, 2.99, 3.27, 3.69, 3.77, 4.03]}, {"scene": "abode", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "links[1]"], "text": "Over two years, what did it grant NPH Action Fund?", "t0": 31.09, "t1": 33.74, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City departments", "sub": "$74.1 million, fiscal 2019 to 2026"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Abode Services", "sub": "a City-funded charity"}, {"art": "money", "name": "NPH Action Fund", "sub": "an advocacy group"}], "kicker": "From the charity’s own tax return"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.38, 0.63, 0.77, 0.9, 0.99, 1.25, 1.68, 1.98]}, {"scene": "abode", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "links[1]"], "text": "175,000 dollars.", "t0": 33.74, "t1": 35.73, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$175,000", "label": "to NPH Action Fund, years to June 2024 and 2025", "sub": "two spellings, one tax number"}, "emph": ["175,000"], "wt": [0.04, 0.22, 0.48, 1.07, 1.41]}, {"scene": "abode", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "links[1]"], "text": "Its stated purpose: promote affordable housing development.", "t0": 36.25, "t1": 38.87, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "PROMOTE AFFORDABLE HOUSING DEVELOPMENT"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.48, 1.23, 1.57, 1.95, 2.23]}, {"scene": "abode", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[1]", "story[3]"], "text": "Three more City-funded charities gave it money too: 270,000 dollars from four in all.", "t0": 38.99, "t1": 43.52, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "$270,000", "label": "to NPH Action Fund from four City-funded charities", "sub": "Abode Services $175,000; Tenants and Owners Development Corporation $50,000; United Way of the Bay Area $25,000; Tides Center $20,000"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.37, 0.84, 1.19, 1.33, 1.42, 1.63, 2.36, 2.56, 2.82, 3.11, 3.41, 3.67, 3.88, 4.15, 4.25]}, {"scene": "abode", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[8]"], "text": "The committee’s own receipts confirm 200,000 dollars of those grants.", "t0": 43.64, "t1": 46.59, "shot": "r15", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$200,000", "label": "matched receipts in the political committee’s account"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.45, 0.61, 0.97, 1.3, 1.46, 1.69, 1.98, 2.25, 2.33, 2.51]}, {"scene": "abode", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "Five organizations match City payees by name and ZIP code. Together they gave 805,000 dollars.", "t0": 46.71, "t1": 52.12, "shot": "r16", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$805,000", "label": "contributions from five matched organizations"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.87, 1.09, 1.31, 1.64, 1.81, 2.07, 2.23, 2.46, 3.23, 3.58, 3.7, 3.9, 4.08, 4.4, 4.67, 4.98]}, {"scene": "abode", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "The Fund’s returns show 19.4 million dollars raised in three years.", "t0": 52.24, "t1": 55.62, "shot": "b9d", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$19.4 million", "label": "contributions on NPH Action Fund’s own returns, 2022 to 2024", "sub": "the four charities’ $270,000: about 1.4%"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.36, 0.76, 0.99, 1.31, 1.52, 1.73, 2.0, 2.29, 2.5, 2.59, 2.8]}, {"scene": "abode", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "The charities gave about 1.4 percent.", "t0": 55.74, "t1": 57.55, "shot": "b9d", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$19.4 million", "label": "contributions on NPH Action Fund’s own returns, 2022 to 2024", "sub": "the four charities’ $270,000: about 1.4%"}, "emph": ["1.4 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.42, 0.59, 0.81, 0.97, 1.17, 1.37]}, {"scene": "coleman", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "links[2]", "links[3]"], "text": "Next, Coleman Children & Youth Services. The City paid it 1.7 million dollars.", "t0": 57.77, "t1": 62.48, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City departments", "sub": "$1.7 million, fiscal 2019 to 2026"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Coleman Children & Youth Services", "sub": "a City-funded charity"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Coleman Action Fund", "sub": "an advocacy group"}], "kicker": "From the charity’s own tax return"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.66, 1.01, 1.33, 1.46, 1.66, 2.55, 2.71, 2.97, 3.19, 3.33, 3.52, 3.73, 3.98, 4.24]}, {"scene": "coleman", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "oneLine"], "text": "From 2021 to 2025, it gave 100,000 dollars to an advocacy group sharing its name.", "t0": 62.6, "t1": 68.03, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Coleman Children & Youth Services", "the charity"], "b": ["Coleman Action Fund", "its namesake advocacy group, $100,000"]}, "emph": ["100,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.46, 0.87, 0.96, 1.19, 2.08, 2.22, 2.44, 2.62, 2.84, 3.15, 3.77, 3.93, 4.03, 4.51, 4.74, 5.03, 5.18]}, {"scene": "coleman", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "Coleman Action Fund. The stated purpose: general support.", "t0": 68.15, "t1": 71.17, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Coleman Children & Youth Services", "the charity"], "b": ["Coleman Action Fund", "its namesake advocacy group, $100,000"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.65, 1.3, 1.45, 1.77, 2.39, 2.7]}, {"scene": "tides", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "links[4]"], "text": "Then Tides Center. The City paid it the most of the three: 104.7 million dollars.